"scoID":["2-s2.0-85120508253"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","prehospital emergency medical services"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b1503f12-e5c3-46c7-ad7f-6ad66f9318ee","au-f7cf8ab9-289b-42bd-a5d9-1591b7f15fe7","ku-0e674c0b-7d3c-4842-9e13-dee8524a191d","sdu-fcbff8b2-4b83-4951-9013-3382acc559e5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Waking Up in Pain : a prospective unselected cohort study of pain in 3702 patients immediately after surgery in the Danish Realm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.89-008547","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The objective was to investigate, first, whether six weeks of intensive ballet dance exposure is associated with structural and clinical changes in the Achilles tendon; second, the importance of demographics, self-reported Achilles pain, and generalized joint hypermobility (GJH). Data were collected at baseline and at six weeks’ follow-up, using Achilles tendon ultrasound tissue characteristics (UTC) as primary outcome (percentage distribution of echo-type I–IV: type I = intact and aligned bundles, type II = discontinuous/wavy bundles, type III = fibrillar, and type IV = amorphous cells/fluid). Secondary outcomes included clinical signs of Achilles tendinopathy, Achilles tendon pain during single-leg heel raise, self-reported symptoms (VISA-A questionnaire), and GJH. Sixty-three ballet dancers (aged 18–41) participated. From baseline to follow-up, UTC echo-type I decreased significantly (β = −3.6, p = 0.001; 95% CI: −5.8;−1.4), whereas echo-type II increased significantly (β = 3.2, p < 0.0001, 95% CI: 1.6;4.8). Furthermore, a significant effect of limb (left limb showed decreased echo-type I and increased echo-type III + IV) and sex (women showed decreased echo-type I and increased in type II) was found. No significant changes in the remaining secondary outcomes were found. Ballet dancers showed structural changes in UTC, corresponding to a decreased echo-type I distribution after six weeks of rehearsing for Swan Lake ballet. No changes in self-reported symptoms, clinical signs of Achilles tendinopathy, and single-leg heel raise test were seen from pre- to post-rehearsal. Thus, UTC changes in the Achilles tendon seem to appear earlier than clinical signs of tendinopathy.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Anker-Petersen, Charlotte","Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","Antflick, Jarrod","Aagaard, Henrik","Myers, Christopher","Boesen, Anders Ploug","Boyle, Eleanor","Hölmich, Per","Thorborg, Kristian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-041571"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Anker-Petersen, Charlotte"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Complete Physio","Tendon Performance"],"keyword":["Achilles Tendon diagnostic imaging","Adolescent","Adult","Dance","Dancing physiology","Diagnostic imaging","Female","Humans","Male","Physical activity","Self Report","Tendinopathy","Ultrasonography","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"six weeks of intensive rehearsals for the swan lake ballet shows ultrasound tissue characterization changes of the achilles tendons in dancers","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191305033/sms.14034.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-041571","identifier":[{"id":"85113588331","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34407248","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-39ee36c1-f4e1-447e-9989-340596f682a4","sdu-5f5e7566-3b1d-4278-9669-028b11a94cec"],"keyword":["Achilles Tendon/diagnostic imaging","Adolescent","Adult","Dancing/physiology","Female","Humans","Male","Self Report","Ultrasonography","Young Adult","dance","diagnostic imaging","physical activity","tendinopathy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-67D8594B4051ECF6996C7BA4D2546A03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/333690860/sms.14034_2_25.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191305033/sms.14034.pdf","version":"A