 of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Musculoskeletal Function and Physiotherapy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, Copenhagen University Hospital Amager and Hvidovre, Hvidovre, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"tendon performance","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Tendon Performance","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"ankerpetersenpau","last":"Anker-Petersen","locid":"cf566f14-3bd2-48c1-9bd5-55305970ccf9","name":"Anker-Petersen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"thorborgpau","last":"Thorborg","name":"Thorborg, Kristian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jarrod","key":"antflickpau","last":"Antflick","name":"Antflick, Jarrod","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","name":"Aagaard, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Chris","key":"myerspau","last":"Myers","name":"Myers, Chris","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Ploug","key":"boesenpau","last":"Boesen","name":"Boesen, Anders Ploug","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"hölmichpau","last":"Hölmich","name":"Hölmich, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"juulkristensenpau","last":"Juul-Kristensen","locid":"887ddfe7-cfa6-4b72-a17d-ecf86987c5c0","name":"Juul-Kristensen, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0002-4973-8415","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bjsports-2019-scandinavianabs.26","issn":["03063674","14730480"],"issn_org":["03063674"],"issue":"Suppl. 1","journal":"British Journal of Sports Medicine","paperid":"26","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-be7665eb-2b6f-4e5e-9aee-53f9ae26ec65"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"After six-weeks of intensive ballet rehearsals changes in the achilles tendons structure appear whereas self-reported severity scores remain the same","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627813","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To describe and demonstrate a simple and secure procedure for laparoscopic autotransplantation of fragmented ovarian cortical tissue in women with diminished ovarian reserve as part of in vitro activation (IVA) of ovarian follicles. Design: Step-by-step video explanation of the surgical procedure with still pictures and surgical video clips to demonstrate the detailed technique. Setting: Fertility clinic and obstetrics and gynecology department at a university hospital. Patient(s): Women with idiopathic diminished ovarian reserve and indication for in vitro fertilization (IVF), aged 25 to 39 years with an antral follicle count bilaterally of ≤5, antimüllerian hormone level of ≤5 pmol/L, and two ovaries. Intervention(s): The laparoscopic autotransplantation consists of six steps: [1] obtaining ovarian cortical biopsy samples, [2] preparing the peritoneal pocket, [3] fragmenting the ovarian cortical tissue into pieces of approximately 1 mm 3 , [4] installing the tissue fragments into a catheter, [5] transplanting the tissue fragments into the peritoneal pocket, and [6] closing the peritoneal pocket with a surgical clip. After the procedure, the patients are evaluated with blood samples and ultrasound scans followed by controlled ovarian stimulation. Ethics committee approval was obtained. Main Outcome Measure(s): Feasibility of a six-step laparoscopic autotransplantation procedure using fragmented ovarian cortical tissue. Result(s): A simple, fast laparoscopic procedure for taking biopsy samples and autotransplanting cortical tissue fragments in an all-in-one procedure ensures the rapid handling and correct placement of the small tissue fragments. The procedure is performed in an outpatient setting with an operation time of 1 hour. We have performed this procedure on 20 patients with no complications. Conclusion(s): In vitro activation is a new, developing option for women in fertility treatment who have diminished ovarian reserve. Fragmentation of murine ovarian tissue has shown to suppress the Hippo pathway, thereby initiating proliferation and growth. This surgical procedure resembles that used when transplanting pieces of frozen-thawed ovarian tissue for fertility restoration, but the fragmented ovarian tissue is only 1 mm 3 , which makes it difficult to transplant. Until now no surgical procedures for transplanting small IVA fragments of cortical tissue has been published. With this video we report in detail a simple way of autotransplanting small fragments of IVA cortical tissue using what is already accessible in the operating theater. Among the many advantages of this procedure are its short duration (1 hour) and outpatient setting, which enable fast recovery and minimal postoperative pain. The procedure also allows fast handling and minimal manipulation of the tissue (limited to the fragmentation). The effect of autotransplantation of fragmented tissue in women with diminished ovarian reserve is currently being studied in ongoing trials. If the technique is combined with chemical IVA, a better outcome may be seen.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lunding, Stine Aagaard","Pors, Susanne Elisabeth","Kristensen, Stine Gry","Andersen, Claus Yding","Jeppesen, Janni Vikkelsø","Macklon, Kirsten Tryde","Andersen, Anders Nyboe","Pedersen, Anette Tønnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-454155"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autotransplantation","Laparoscopy","Premature ovarian failure","diminished ovarian reserve"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autotransplantation of fragmented ovarian cortical tissue a laparoscopic demonstration","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-454155","identifier":[{"id":"85055900319","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30396563","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-65a499b3-80cd-4e68-a441-9dd8b7f40b3b"],"keyword":["Autotransplantation","diminished ovarian reserve","in vitro activation","laparoscopy","premature ovarian failure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-61254785B42C2D1FDF68E7E291E1AB0F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stine Aagaard","key":"lundingstineaagaardpau","last":"Lunding","name":"Lunding, Stine Aagaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne Elisabeth","key":"porssusanneelisabethpau","last":"Pors","name":"Pors, Susanne Elisabeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine Gry","key":"kristensenstinegrypau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Stine Gry","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Claus Yding","key":"andersenclausydingpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"de926ac7-21b1-4c38-8d85-3c8e45cd483a","name":"Andersen, Claus Yding","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janni Vikkelsø","key":"jeppesenjannivikkelsøpau","last":"Jeppesen","name":"Jeppesen, Janni Vikkelsø","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten Tryde","key":"macklonkirstentrydepau","last":"Macklon","name":"Macklon, Kirsten Tryde","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Nyboe","key":"andersenandersnyboepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4b63bd7a-c8eb-4de4-a751-6ed71ba80cb4","name":"Andersen, Anders Nyboe","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anette Tønnes","key":"pedersenanettetønnespau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"de173c3f-f7b8-47fb-b3c4-6138fa53337c","name":"Pedersen, Anette Tønnes","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30396563"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fertnstert.2018.08.024","issn":["00150282","15462501"],"issn_org":["00150282"],"issue":"6","journal":"Fertility and Sterility","pages":"1181-1183","status":"p","title":"Fertility and Sterility","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055900319"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-65a499b3-80cd-4e68-a441-9dd8b7f40b3b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Autotransplantation of fragmented ovarian cortical tissue : a laparoscopic demonstration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-454155","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Dalton is a powerful general-purpose program system for the study of molecular electronic structure at the Hartree–Fock, Kohn–Sham, multiconfigurational self-consistent-field, Møller–Plesset, configuration-interaction, and coupled-cluster levels of theory. Apart from the total energy, a wide variety of molecular properties may be calculated using these electronic-structure models. Molecular gradients and Hessians are available for geometry optimizations, molecular dynamics, and vibrational studies, whereas magnetic resonance and optical activity can be studied in a gauge-origin-invariant manner. Frequency-dependent molecular properties can be calculated using linear, quadratic, and cubic response theory. A large number of singlet and triplet perturbation operators are available for the study of one-, two-, and three-photon processes. Environmental effects may be included using various dielectric-medium and quantum-mechanics/molecular-mechanics models. Large molecules may be studied using linear-scaling and massively parallel algorithms. Dalton is distributed at no cost from http://www.daltonprogram.org for a number of UNIX platforms.","author_count":158,"contributors":["Aidas, Kestutis","Angeli, C.","Bak, Keld L.","Bakken, V.","Bast, R.","Boman, L.","Christiansen, Ove","Cimiraglia, R.","Coriani, S.","Dahle, P.","Dalskov, E.K.","Ekström, U.","Enevoldsen, T.","Eriksen, Janus Juul","Ettenhuber, Patrick","Fernández, B.","Ferrighi, L.","Fliegl, H.","Frediani, L.","Hald, K.","Halkier, A.","Hättig, C.","Heiberg, H.","Helgaker, T.","Hennum, A.C.","Hettema, H.","Hjertenæs, E.","Høst, Stinne","Høyvik, Ida-Marie","Iozzi, M.F.","Jansík, B.","Jensen, H.J.A.","Jonsson, D.","Jørgensen, Poul","Kauczor, J.","Kirpekar, S.","Kjærgaard, Thomas","Klopper, W.","Knecht, Stefan","Kobayashi, R.","Koch, H.","Kongsted, J.","Krapp, A.","Kristensen, Kasper","Ligabue, A.","Lutnæs, O.B.","Melo, J.I.","Mikkelsen, K.V.","Myhre, R.H.","Neiss, C.","Nielsen, C.B.","Norman, P.","Olsen, Jeppe","Olsen, J.M.H.","Osted, A.","Packer, M.J.","Pawlowski, F.","Pedersen, T.B.","Provasi, P.F.","Reine, S.","Rinkevicius, Z.","Ruden, T.A.","Ruud, K.","Rybkin, V.V.","Sałek, P.","Samson, C.C.M.","de Merás, A.S.","Saue, T.","Sauer, Stephan P. A.","Schimmelpfennig, B.","Sneskov, K.","Steindal, A.H.","Sylvester-Hvid, K. O.","Taylor, P.R.","Teale, A.M.","Tellgren, E.I.","Tew, D.P.","Thorvaldsen, A.J.","Thøgersen, L.","Vahtras, O.","Watson, M.A.","Wilson, Douglas","Ziolkowski, M.","Ågren, H."],"cuid":["S03-099.52-014628"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Argentina","Australia","Czechia","France","Germany","Italy","Lithuania","New Zealand","Norway","Poland","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University","Cisco Systems, Lysaker","Clemson University","CoE for Next Generation Computing, Clemson University","Department of Philosophy, University of Auckland","Department of Physics, University of Northeastern and IMIT-CONICET","Department of Physiotherapy, Faculty of Medicine, Nursing and Health Sciences, Victori","Department of Theoretical Chemistry, Ruhr–University Bochum","EMGS ASA, Trondheim","Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nürnberg","Institute of Physical Chemistry, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Jotun A/S, Sandefjord","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","Kazimierz Wielki University","Kjeller Software Community, Oslo","La Trobe University","Linköping University","Norwegian Computing Center, Oslo","Norwegian Defence Research Establishment, Kjeller","Norwegian Meteorological Institute","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","PSS9 Development, Cracow","Paul Sabatier University","Physics Department, FCEyN-UBA and IFIBA, Ciudad Universitaria, o